{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Add the self-contained rebar MCP HTTP service to the box per the ADR (deft-evolutive-mosasaur):\na new `mcp` compose service + `Dockerfile.mcp` running loopback-published `rebar-mcp` HTTP, and an\nnginx `/mcp/` TLS-edge location with a **switchable upstream** so the autodeploy slice\n(panicky-sylphish-foxterrier) can flip traffic blue→green atomically. INFRA only; the live AWS\nprovision/deploy is approval-gated (a human performs it). Single concern: the on-box MCP service\nand its edge — autodeploy logic lives in foxterrier, secrets in avians.\n\n## Scope\n- `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml`: an `mcp` service (image built from `Dockerfile.mcp`),\n  loopback-published on host `127.0.0.1:8091` (Gerrit owns 8080, review-bot REVIEW_BOT_PORT,\n  opcert 8090), `restart: always`, a container `healthcheck` hitting the MCP `/health` endpoint,\n  and `stop_grace_period: 1260s` (covers the 1200s app SIGTERM grace below + margin, so Docker\n  never escalates SIGTERM→SIGKILL mid-op). ADR-decided fail-closed HTTP posture via env:\n  `REBAR_MCP_TRANSPORT=http`, `REBAR_MCP_HTTP_HOST=0.0.0.0`, `REBAR_MCP_HTTP_PORT=8091`,\n  `REBAR_MCP_HTTP_TLS_AT_EDGE=true`, `REBAR_MCP_HTTP_ALLOWED_HOSTS`/`REBAR_MCP_HTTP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS`\n  (the external host / origin), `REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ENABLED=1`, `REBAR_MCP_AUTH_STRATEGIES=static`,\n  `REBAR_MCP_AUTH_RESOURCE_SERVER_URL`, `REBAR_MCP_AUTH_STATIC_TOKENS_FILE`. `MCP_PATHS` for the\n  autodeploy change-detector is declared here (a compose comment) so foxterrier can consume it.\n- `infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp` (NEW): builds `rebar-mcp` from the same repo-root build context +\n  committed `uv.lock` as `Dockerfile.opcert` (`python:3.12-slim`,\n  `uv sync --locked --no-dev --extra agents --extra mcp`). CMD boots `rebar-mcp` (http transport\n  via the compose env). A container `HEALTHCHECK` curls the loopback `/health`.\n- `infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template`: a new `location /mcp/` proxying to a named `upstream rebar_mcp`\n  block whose `server` line is a **materialized include** `include /etc/nginx/mcp-upstream*.conf;`\n  (the atomic-flip seam). TLS terminates at nginx (mirrors `/review/` + `/opcert/`).\n- `infra/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf` (NEW, committed seed): the initial (blue) target\n  `server 127.0.0.1:8091;`.\n- `infra/scripts/materialize-mcp-upstream.sh` (NEW): the concrete, committed fresh-boot installer.\n  It copies the committed seed `infra/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf` to `/etc/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf`\n  ONLY IF that target is absent (so a later foxterrier blue→green rewrite is never clobbered on a\n  redeploy), then `nginx -s reload`. Mirrors the `materialize-opcert-guard.sh` SSM→file precedent\n  in shape (a local-file seed here — no SSM). It is idempotent and re-runnable.\n- `infra/scripts/compose-up.sh`: call `materialize-mcp-upstream.sh` BEFORE `docker compose up`,\n  beside the existing `materialize-opcert-guard.sh` call, with the same non-fatal WARN pattern.\n- A `/health` endpoint on the MCP server exposing an integer `in_flight` gauge that counts ONLY\n  long-running/certified ops (review_plan/verify_completion/review_code/scan_spec), plus a bounded\n  SIGTERM grace window so a retiring container lets an in-flight op finish before exit. The gauge\n  feeds foxterrier's retire check; it does not gate the deploy. New health/gauge/signal code lives\n  in a NEW module `src/rebar/_mcp_health.py` (mcp_server.py is at its 800-LOC cap), wired from\n  `build_server`/`main`.\n\n## nginx switchable-upstream: grounded fresh-boot + atomic flip\nUnlike the `/opcert/` guard `map` (whose `default 0` makes a zero-match GLOB include safe), an nginx\n`upstream {}` with ZERO `server` lines is a config error (`nginx -t`: \"no servers are inside\nupstream\"). So: (1) the template uses a GLOB include `include /etc/nginx/mcp-upstream*.conf;`\n(zero-match-tolerant, mirroring the `opcert-guard*.conf` glob shape); (2) this change ships the\ncommitted seed `infra/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf`; and (3) a NEW committed installer\n`infra/scripts/materialize-mcp-upstream.sh`, wired into `infra/scripts/compose-up.sh` next to the\nopcert-guard materialize, copies that seed to `/etc/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf` (only if absent) before\nthe stack comes up, so a fresh boot has exactly one backend (127.0.0.1:8091) and `nginx -t` passes.\n(Correction: no committed script renders `rebar.conf.template` via `envsubst` today — that appears\nonly as an example comment in the template header — and `/etc/nginx/opcert-guard.map.conf` is written\nby `materialize-opcert-guard.sh` via SSM, a different mechanism; this plan does NOT rely on either.\nThe seed installer above is the grounded, committed step.) foxterrier's blue→green cutover re-points\nby atomically rewriting that single `/etc/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf` + `nginx -s reload`. The AC's\n`nginx -t` verification renders the template WITH the seed include present.\n\n## /health is exempt from bearer auth\n`/health` is registered as a FastMCP `custom_route` (a Starlette route on the Streamable-HTTP app),\nwhich sits OUTSIDE the SDK's `RequireAuthMiddleware` (that middleware guards only the mounted MCP\nendpoint, not sibling custom routes). So under `REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ENABLED=1` an unauthenticated\ncontainer HEALTHCHECK / nginx probe of `/health` still returns 200 (no bearer required); only `/mcp`\nenforces the `static` bearer. A test asserts `/health` → 200 with auth ENABLED and no token.\n\n## SIGTERM grace (concrete numbers)\n`src/rebar/_mcp_health.py` defines `DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS = 1200` (a module constant, the\nreview-bot `review_bot/config.py` budget precedent — not a rebar config key). On SIGTERM the process\nwaits up to 1200s for the `in_flight` gauge to reach 0, then exits; the compose `stop_grace_period:\n1260s` covers it. The SIGTERM AC asserts against these numbers.\n\n## Approach + rationale\nMirror the proven opcert edge (loopback service + nginx location) but expose a switchable upstream\nrather than a hardcoded `proxy_pass host:port`, because the ADR's blue-green cutover needs to\nre-point the upstream atomically (the local updater's `current`-pointer analog). `/health` counts\nonly expensive ops so retirement waits on billable work, not trivial reads. Shared base image keeps\ndisk/build cost low; the extra retained MCP images are bounded by the existing docker prune.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tier: **in-process ASGI integration** (docker NOT required): `/health` served by the FastMCP\n  `streamable_http_app` returns a JSON body with an integer `in_flight` field. Oracle: `in_flight`\n  reads 0 at idle, increments while a simulated long-running certified op runs (a stubbed certified\n  tool held in flight), and returns to 0 after — asserted via the real endpoint through a Starlette\n  TestClient; a trivial read op does NOT move the gauge (contrast case). `/health` also returns 200\n  WITHOUT a bearer while `REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ENABLED=1` (auth-exemption oracle).\n- [ ] Fail-closed boot: with a non-loopback bind and NO TLS-at-edge/allowlist ack, `build_server`\n  refuses to start (raises `McpStartupError` with the ADR-0050 guard message); with the ack it\n  boots. Oracle: the existing `_resolve_http_runtime` gates, asserted directly.\n- [ ] The nginx `/mcp/` location proxies to a named `upstream rebar_mcp` block whose `server` line\n  is sourced from the materialized include `mcp-upstream*.conf`; the committed seed\n  `infra/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf` supplies `server 127.0.0.1:8091;`; and\n  `infra/scripts/materialize-mcp-upstream.sh` (called from `compose-up.sh`) installs the seed to\n  `/etc/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf` only-if-absent. Oracle: structural parse of the rendered template\n  + the committed seed + the installer wiring (nginx binary not required in CI; `nginx -t` when a\n  binary is available).\n- [ ] SIGTERM grace: with the `in_flight` gauge > 0, a SIGTERM lets the op finish (the process does\n  NOT exit immediately) and exits 0 once the gauge drains, within the 1200s bound — asserted by a\n  subprocess/signal test driving the `_mcp_health` grace handler; and `stop_grace_period` (1260s) ≥\n  `DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS` (1200s), asserted structurally over compose + the module.\n\n## Testing\nIn-process ASGI tests (Starlette TestClient over `streamable_http_app`) for `/health`\nidle/inflight/contrast + the auth-exemption; direct `build_server` assertions for the fail-closed\ngates; a structural parse of the rendered nginx template + seed + installer wiring; a\nsubprocess/signal test for the SIGTERM grace window; a numeric assertion tying `stop_grace_period`\nto `DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS`. No docker dependency.\n\n## File impact\n`infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp` (new), `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml`,\n`infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template`, `infra/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf` (new),\n`infra/scripts/materialize-mcp-upstream.sh` (new), `infra/scripts/compose-up.sh`,\n`src/rebar/_mcp_health.py` (new), `src/rebar/mcp_server.py`, and tests under `tests/`.\n\n## Compat / rollback\nPurely additive — new service, new port, new nginx location; touches no existing service. Rollback =\nremove the `mcp` service/location + seed include + installer call (gerrit/review-bot/opcert\nunaffected). Security trust-boundary: new authenticated network endpoint — enforced by `static`\nbearer at the app (`/mcp`) + TLS at the nginx edge; `/health` is intentionally unauthenticated\n(no secrets, only an integer gauge).\n\nDepends on: deft-evolutive-mosasaur (ADR). Blocks: panicky-sylphish-foxterrier (needs the\nswitchable upstream + `/health`), unmythical-uninspired-olm (needs a reachable endpoint)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787612489633902001,"uuid":"1bbad667-2e96-41cd-afd9-852da624db47"}